      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRCX keeps an eye out for changes to friends list and keeps a log of when changes happen.\n\nI think tracking the start of a friendship could be interesting to work out. Like in a situation where I send you a friend request, does VRChat need to keep track of when it was issued, or maybe when it was accepted.\n\nPersonally I don't typically accept friend requests immediately because I think some people just see a white name tag and then send a friend request. Most recently I initially met someone who was in the middle of a discussion about food that I kinda walked away from because it was boring, but I later accepted it like 40 days later. Would VRChat record the information for the first interaction, or the second?\n\nThe other one to worry about is if I have a good time with someone, I crash, and then I send them a friend request when I'm logged back into my home world. Will their info show that we met in my home world?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
